From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:52:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: one Pro Controller is one pad: IOHIDManager hands a
 device over once per matching dictionary it meets, so the HID reader knows a
 pad by its I/O Registry entry, not by its IOHIDDeviceRef (PR #1722)

A Pro Controller meets both the GamePad usage dictionary and the vendor / product one added for identical pads (PR #1595), and each match came as a new
IOHIDDeviceRef for the same registry entry. hidpad_found compared references only, so one pad counted as two of its model against GameController's one
controller: both were read as twins, players 1 and 2. A one-player game then opened the controller applet every few frames, and The Legend of Zelda:
Ocarina of Time, which suspends its music while an applet has focus, played no area or cutscene music.

Co-authored-by: Ludovic LEMARINEL - Adesin.fr <10656218+LudovicLemarinel@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit a00f03bb3f7275c3f897df5834e2d6da91783992)

